From: substrate
Subject: kdrive: default to evdev on /dev/input/event0

Plain `Xfbdev vt1 -retro` launched with no -mouse/-keybd leaves
kdConfigPointers and kdConfigKeyboards empty, so KdInitInput's loops
add no devices and the X server runs without input.  On substrate the
only working input path is the evdev backend on /dev/input/event0;
make that the default when the user didn't ask for anything else.

Anyone who *does* pass -mouse/-keybd keeps full control: the fallback
only fires when the config-device lists are empty.

--- a/hw/kdrive/src/kinput.c
+++ b/hw/kdrive/src/kinput.c
@@ -1265,6 +1265,15 @@ KdInitInput(void)

     kdInputEnabled = TRUE;

+    /* substrate default: if the user didn't pass -mouse / -keybd, wire
+     * up the evdev driver on /dev/input/event0 so a bare `Xfbdev vt1
+     * -retro` actually has working input.  Without this, kdConfigPointers
+     * and kdConfigKeyboards are empty and the X server runs deviceless. */
+    if (!kdConfigPointers)
+        KdAddConfigPointer("evdev,,device=/dev/input/event0");
+    if (!kdConfigKeyboards)
+        KdAddConfigKeyboard("evdev,,device=/dev/input/event0");
+
     for (dev = kdConfigPointers; dev; dev = dev->next) {
         pi = KdParsePointer(dev->line);
         if (!pi)
